{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793458225,"nonce":"OXAHT1eXedqP68lT+oB+6PpNtA4=","title":"Lua tokenize: where the 3.3x behind LuaJIT goes","message":"At 7a709d93 (Mac, quiet run): tokenize 122.7 ms wall / 102.4 elapsed, LuaJIT 37.0 / 31.9.\n\nSplit into its three phases (5 passes each over the kernel's 300000 tokens, Mac under load, so ratios rather than times): gmatch over \"[^ ]+\" 63 ms vs LuaJIT 25 (2.5x); counting into a string-keyed table, `counts[tok] = (counts[tok] or 0) + 1`, 40 to 73 ms vs 0.5 (80x and more); building the parts with `..` and tostring 51 to 55 ms vs 9 (6x).\n\nA sample of 80 repetitions of main (JIT addresses attributed): of the active time, about a quarter is the collector's marking (Marker::consider, drain_to, slab_bits, collect_from) and about a third the pattern engine (match_bracket_class, do_match, single_match, class_end, host_pat_match_at), then zyntax_alloc, memmove, string hash and equality.\n\n- Counting: `counts` is an empty constructor with string keys, so its values live boxed in the hash part; the read joins nil, `or 0` makes it dynamic, the `+ 1` takes the dynamic path and the store boxes again. The likely bulk is a box per store, which also feeds the collector. LuaJIT's interned strings make the probe a pointer compare and its values are unboxed numbers.\n- gmatch: the engine is lstrlib's algorithm (as LuaJIT's is), so the difference is per match: two match attempts per token (one fails at the space), a fresh Matcher with a 32-entry capture array each time, and several thread-local RefCell reads of the result per token. A bracket class is also re-read for every byte it tests.\n- Building: string concatenation and tostring allocate each piece.\n\nDirections: a hash part typed by its values (an integer-valued string map stores i64, no box) or boxes that do not allocate for integers; one Matcher kept per gmatch walk and the result read without thread-local round trips; a bracket class turned into a byte set once per match.","files":null}]}